# An unknown head whose tail begins with a known method defines a named Structure and
# calls nothing (Q58; the author, 2026-10-05; docs/LMX_semantics.en.md#construction):
# `s: shout` retains the application of shout in the body of s without executing it,
# so shout prints nothing. report prints DONE (a C door keeps it native when the root
# is walked) and gives 7. The program says only DONE. Entry 7.
fn: shout () int
    c.printf: "called\n"
    return: 1

fn: report () int
    c.printf: "DONE\n"
    return: 7
end: report

s: shout
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: report(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
